Unbinding the running thread leaves the timer where it was.
A thread alone on the processor that loses its share would run on to a tick set for it alone;
the timer is set past a tick only while no change since has brought that tick forward.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the timer is set past a tick an unmarked change brought forward

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -322,7 +322,6 @@ void sched_bind(struct thread *t, uint32_t share, struct cap *parent)
 
 void sched_unbind(struct cap *bound)
 {
-    wake_stale = true;
     struct thread *t = bound_thread(bound);
     if (t->state == THREAD_READY && t != current) {
         dequeue(t);
